# Files that should NEVER end up in the ZIP we distribute via wordpress.org.
# `git archive` respects `export-ignore`, so the artifact stays clean even
# if we change the build pipeline later.
#
# Note: dot-files are forbidden by the wordpress.org automated plugin scan
# ("hidden_files: Hidden files are not permitted"). The list below covers
# what currently lives in the repo plus the most common dot-files / dev-only
# files that could sneak in over time.

.gitignore       export-ignore
.gitattributes   export-ignore
.github          export-ignore
.editorconfig    export-ignore
.vscode          export-ignore
.idea            export-ignore
.DS_Store        export-ignore
Thumbs.db        export-ignore

# Dev-only top-level docs (wp.org uses readme.txt, not README.md).
# README.md is kept for GitHub but you can flip the line below if you'd
# rather not ship it. Currently we DO ship it -- it does no harm.
# README.md      export-ignore

# Tests / fixtures / CI configs would go here too when we add them:
# tests/         export-ignore
# phpunit.xml    export-ignore
# composer.lock  export-ignore
